Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-14-2000||02:13 PM||||Well its been a LONG 7 months, but shes about finished (with exception of side decals and painting the wheels)...<BR>To give you an idea of what I had to work with..heres some before pics...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MyFieroBeforeA.jpg">  <BR>EEK!!! The car had been wrecked in the front, and had been painted FOUR times! Among other things, I had to repair the front, put on a new nose, strip off ALL the old paint, and of course repaint...<BR>Heres another...<BR>BEFORE...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MyFieroBeforeC.jpg">  <BR>One more BEFORE...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MyFieroBeforeD.jpg">  <P>Here she is NOW!!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-009f_2.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-011f_1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-010f_1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-013f.jpg">  <BR>The color is 2000 Plymouth Prowler red...<BR>Needless to say, there were MANY MANY more things I had to do to this car, but, it was worth it!! Also, my roommate and I did all the work, even the painting! However, I think I'll shy away from Fieros needing this much work again for some time!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-14-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||2xsess||10-14-2000||02:57 PM||||It looks really sharp, I like the color!!!!<P><B>Good Job!!!!</B><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||10-14-2000||04:06 PM||||It looks sweet, but I am curious why did you go with the different nose?  I though the original nose was better for aerodynamics especially at high speeds.<P>PS Thanks for fixing those sail panels...  that just didnt look right before!||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||10-14-2000||04:52 PM||||Thanx...Greg Piet, I changed the nose because it was the incorrect nose for that model. When I bought it, it had a GT nose on it..since its a Formula, I was restoring it back to pretty much original (with the exception of the color)..besides, all my other Fiero's have the GT/SE nose on them.<BR>The Formula originally had the coupe nose on it when produced.<BR>oh yeah, the sail panel windows were replaced w/ new ones (boneyard actually), the old ones were toast w/ that stupid paint on them.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||10-14-2000||05:17 PM||||The car is beautiful.Isn't it a great feeling when you are done?I spent 5 years on my Chevelle,and the thing I remember most is the time I stepped back away from the car and there was nothing else to do. ||||reg||1
